
Contents of "cnet:mail/fido/"

    ClearAcct

        - This file is launched from the "NetUtils" file from within CNet
          to clear the accounting statistics for all nodes that have called
          you for Freq'ing purposes.

    DoTick.rexx

        - The ARexx script launched from the "Poll-Script2" main polling
          script to process incoming tick files. Edit the values found in
          this file to match your systems needs.

    ENumNet

        - Another utility used by the "NetUtils" file. This utility searches
          your nodelist and displays all know systems within a certain
          region.

    GetNode

        - Also launched from the "NetUtils" file. This program takes a FIDO
          address(supplied by you) and shows you all data pertaining to that
          address as found in the current NodeList.

    ListAcct

        - Last utility launched from "NetUtils". This one lists all systems
          that have accounting statistics on file for you(used with freqs).

    NodeDiff.rexx

        - ARexx script which processes "NodeDiff" files. After adding it to
          your "NodeList" file, it is copied to your "NODEDIFFS" ud directory
          and will be adopted into the base by CNet's AMaint that night. In
          the file, you'll see how to change things if they differ from your
          system.

    Poll.rexx

        - This is an ARexx script which I call the DOS "Poll-Script2" file
          to add entries to the "Poll" log, which is placed in "SysData:Log/"
          directory.

Other Files: (Not included in this archive):

    "cnet:mail/fido/docs/"  directory

        - This is the directory I place all my FIDO doc files, like policies,
          filebone lists, NA and NO lists, etc.

    "cnet:mail/fido/other/" directory

        - This is where I store any other FIDO-type programs I haven't found
          a use for yet, or I haven't figured out HOW to use yet.

